  "rootCause": {
    "confirmed": "The first studio selection starts a real lazy SFC import. The preference test puts that compilation inside vi.waitFor's default one-second polling budget, unlike the existing theme-controller suite which initializes the real theme in beforeAll. A controlled 1500 ms cold transform deterministically reproduces the exact original two-writes/one-write failure.",
    "limit": "The original loaded environment's individual compiler/scheduler timings were not measured. The injected reproduction establishes the faulty timing boundary without claiming a deterministic runtime defect."
  },
  "changes": [
    {
      "path": "packages/music-workbench/test/features/plugins/use-workbench-theme.test.ts",
      "line": 98,
      "detail": "Use the public loadBuiltInTheme in a bounded 20-second beforeAll hook, matching the existing controller suite. The real built-in module is compiled before preference assertions; no loader mock, global timeout change, test retry or assertion removal is introduced."
    }
  ],
